      "message": "\u003e It is just getServices and that users a userId int, not a UserHandle.\n\nThere are few more in the [android.nfc](https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003duserId\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fgoogleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain:frameworks%2Fbase%2Fnfc%2Fjava%2Fandroid%2Fnfc%2F) package\n\n\u003e You\u0027d need android.permission.INTERACT_ACROSS_USERS as a prerequisite for calling this API then; otherwise you\u0027re violating the permission model for cross-user interactions (e.g. see here).\n\nYep, agreed with that suggestion and using `UserHandle` instead of userId.",
